    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29761" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŏsella</span></b> , ae,
		m. and f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river of Belgic Gaul</i>, now the <i>Moselle</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 13,
				53</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. H. 4, 71</span></i>; <i><span class="en">77</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">largus Mosella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. de Clar. Urb. 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">placida Mosella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Idyll. 10, 73</span></i>
			.—Also called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŏsŭla</span></b> , ae,
			f., <i><span class="en">Flor. 3, 10, 14</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŏsellēus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the
				Moselle</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ortus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 1, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
